  "scope": "One disposable stock Kind v0.32.0 cluster with Kubernetes v1.36.1 and kindnet; case-owned synthetic data-store and model-registry/inference Services, one client, and temporary CA/leaf certificates. Each endpoint serves the same fixed marker on HTTP/8080 and TLS/8443 before enforcement. A client egress NetworkPolicy then permits DNS and case endpoint TCP/8443 only. The case checks plaintext baseline retrieval, plaintext-port rejection after policy, trusted TLS with expected service DNS identity, wrong-name rejection, untrusted-CA rejection, and continued marker retrieval over TLS. This tests application TLS verification and port-level egress restriction on these synthetic paths only. It does not prove CNI transparent encryption, storage or registry vendor settings, production workload coverage, RDMA, GPU/NCCL traffic, performance, or encryption of every data path.",
